{
  "id": "xo20ay6",
  "title": "Chapter 5: Output Devices",
  "order": 5,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7exmf6",
      "content": "Output devices are hardware components that present processed data and information from the computer to the user in a human-readable form such as text, images, audio, or printed documents."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Primary Output Categories",
          "value": "Soft Copy & Hard Copy",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Printer Resolution Metric",
          "value": "DPI (Dots Per Inch)",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Printer Speed Metric",
          "value": "PPM / CPS",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Major Monitor Types",
          "value": "CRT, LCD, LED, OLED",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "fyonrke"
    },
    {
      "id": "n1eqsow",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Monitor"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Monitors display visual information as soft copy output, categorized into CRT, LCD, LED, and OLED technologies.",
        "Printers generate permanent physical output (hard copy) and are divided into Impact and Non-Impact printers.",
        "Plotters are specialized output devices designed for vector graphics, blueprint printing, and high-precision CAD drawings.",
        "Speakers convert electronic digital audio signals into audible acoustic sound waves.",
        "Non-impact printers like Laser and Inkjet provide higher speed, superior resolution, and quieter operation compared to impact printers."
      ],
      "id": "knpaybn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ehvt6mj",
      "content": "A monitor is the most common output device used to display visual information generated by a computer. It is also called a Visual Display Unit (VDU)."
    },
    {
      "id": "0jcnn4d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.1 Types of Monitors"
    },
    {
      "id": "tfazyj1",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Monitor Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Technology</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CRT</p>",
            "<p>Cathode Ray Tube</p>",
            "<p>Bulky, heavy, consumes more power.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LCD</p>",
            "<p>Liquid Crystal Display</p>",
            "<p>Flat screen, low power consumption.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LED</p>",
            "<p>Light Emitting Diode</p>",
            "<p>Improved brightness and energy efficiency.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vbfw80x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.2 Monitor Characteristics"
    },
    {
      "id": "xnpkd7d",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Resolution – Number of pixels displayed on the screen.",
        "Refresh Rate – Number of times the screen updates per second.",
        "Pixel – Smallest unit of a digital image.",
        "Aspect Ratio – Ratio of width to height of the display."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hsd8i7h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.2 Printer"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Plotters are specialized output devices used for printing high-quality vector graphics and large-scale engineering drawings.",
      "id": "192za6h"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jcfq7ya",
      "content": "A printer is an output device that produces a hard copy of digital documents on paper."
    },
    {
      "id": "nynung7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.2.1 Types of Printers"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9sxq4q",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Printer Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dot Matrix Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Uses pins to strike ribbon and print characters.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Daisy Wheel Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Produces letter-quality text using wheel-shaped print head.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Line Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Prints one line at a time, used in large organizations.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inkjet Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact</p>",
            "<p>Sprays tiny ink droplets onto paper.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Laser Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact</p>",
            "<p>Uses laser technology and toner for fast printing.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mjrl28b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.2.2 Impact vs Non-Impact Printers"
    },
