          "Physical striking against inked ribbon on paper",
          "Chemical, heat, laser, or ink spray mechanism"
        ],
        [
          "Noise Level",
          "High noise level due to mechanical striking",
          "Very quiet operation"
        ],
        [
          "Speed",
          "Slower (measured in CPS or LPM)",
          "Faster (measured in PPM)"
        ],
        [
          "Print Quality",
          "Lower resolution and basic graphics",
          "High resolution, sharp text, and photographic output"
        ],
        [
          "Examples",
          "Dot Matrix, Daisy Wheel, Line Printer",
          "Laser Printer, Inkjet Printer, Thermal Printer"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "nyvx56e"
    },
    {
      "id": "o8ve6dv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Impact Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact Printer</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Uses mechanical striking</p>",
            "<p>No physical striking</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Noisy</p>",
            "<p>Quiet</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Example: Dot Matrix</p>",
            "<p>Example: Laser Printer</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l28k22z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.3 Plotter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o028qm2",
      "content": "A plotter is a specialized output device used to produce high-quality graphics and technical drawings."
    },
    {
      "id": "6iz9w1g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.3.1 Types of Plotters"
    },
    {
      "id": "h65kruq",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Plotter Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Drum Plotter</p>",
            "<p>Paper moves around a rotating drum while pen draws images.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Flatbed Plotter</p>",
            "<p>Paper remains fixed while pen moves over the surface.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "n8pcf7j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Speaker"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Impact printers (e.g., Dot Matrix) use physical striking mechanisms, while Non-Impact printers (Laser, Inkjet) use non-contact technology.",
        "DPI (Dots Per Inch) determines printer output quality, while PPM (Pages Per Minute) measures printer speed.",
        "Laser printers use electrostatic toner powder and a drum mechanism, making them the fastest non-impact printers for text."
      ],
      "id": "18qujet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l9f4hqt",
      "content": "Speakers are output devices used to produce sound from a computer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2w1zqbi",
      "content": "Common Uses:"
    },
    {
      "id": "krel46a",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Music playback",
        "Video sound",
        "Voice communication",
        "Multimedia applications"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dfdnql0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.5 Important Exam Points"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2k3xcc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Monitor is also called VDU (Visual Display Unit).",
        "CRT stands for Cathode Ray Tube.",
        "LCD stands for Liquid Crystal Display.",
        "LED stands for Light Emitting Diode.",
        "Dot Matrix Printer is an impact printer.",
        "Laser Printer is a non-impact printer.",
        "Plotters are used for engineering and architectural drawings."
      ]
    }
  ],
